We need to build a complete retrosynthesis route JSON. We have template 1914384 with mapped_rxn. Applying template gave [] (no precursors). Maybe need to deprotect? Or need to verify step? The route likely includes the target molecule (from mapped_rxn product). Need to extract product SMILES from mapped_rxn. The mapped_rxn: "([CH3:1]/[C:2]([c:3]1[cH:4][cH:5][cH:6][cH:7][cH:8]1)=[CH:9]/[CH2:10][CH2:11][CH2:12][C:13](=[O:14])[C:15]([F:16])([F:17])[F:18])>>([CH3:1][C@H:2]([c:3]1[cH:4][cH:5][cH:6][cH:7][cH:8]1)[C@@H:9]1[CH2:10][CH2:11][CH2:12][C@@:13]1([OH:14])[C:15]([F:16])([F:17])[F:18])"

Left side is reactant (precursor) and right side is product (target). So target SMILES is the product: "[CH3][C@H]([c]1[cH][cH][cH][cH][cH]1)[C@@H]1[CH2][CH2][CH2][C@@]1([OH])[C]([F])([F])[F]" but need proper SMILES without stereochemistry? Use as given: "[CH3][C@H]([c]1[cH][cH][cH][cH][cH]1)[C@@H]1[CH2][CH2][CH2][C@@]1([OH])[C]([F])([F])[F]". Might need to remove brackets for atoms: CH3 is "C". The product likely is a fluorinated cyclohexanol with aromatic ring. But we can just use the SMILES from mapped_rxn product side.

We need route: root node type mol with smiles target. Then child reaction node with template_id 1914384, children are precursor molecules (list). However apply_template returned empty, meaning maybe no precursors found due to mapping issues. Could be that we need to deprotect? Or maybe the precursor is the left side of mapped_rxn. So we can manually set precursors as the left side SMILES: "([CH3]/[C]([c]1[cH][cH][cH][cH][cH]1)=[CH]/[CH2][CH2][CH2][C](=[O])[C]([F])([F])[F])". That's the reactant.

Thus route: target mol -> reaction using template -> precursor mol.

We need to provide JSON. Use smiles strings as is.

